# Vision Pipeline Diagram

```
Raw Image → Preprocessing → Feature Detection → Object Recognition → Scene Understanding
     ↓            ↓               ↓                  ↓                    ↓
Pixel Array  Noise Reduced   Edges & Corners   Object Labels       Context & Relations
     ↓            ↓               ↓                  ↓                    ↓
  640x480    Color Corrected  Textures & Lines   "Person", "Chair"   "Person Sitting"
```

## Description

This diagram illustrates the multi-stage visual processing pipeline used by robot vision systems. Starting with raw pixel data, the system progressively extracts higher-level semantic information while filtering out irrelevant details. Each stage adds more meaning to the visual input, transforming basic pixel arrays into rich environmental understanding that enables intelligent robot behavior.